  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nHi All,\r\n\r\nWhile trying to understand failures in WPT test case:\r\n\r\nWPT Test Case: https://wpt.fyi/results/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/lists/lists-styles.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=safari%3Afail\r\n\r\nI noticed that we fail following test cases:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<ol type=\"none\"> - list-style-type\t\r\n<ol type=\"NONE\"> - list-style-type\t\r\n<ol type=\"disc\"> - list-style-type\t\r\n<ol type=\"DISC\"> - list-style-type\t\r\n<ol type=\"circle\"> - list-style-type\t\r\n<ol type=\"CIRCLE\"> - list-style-type\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut Web-Spec: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#lists ; only have 'presentational hints' for `ul` and `li` but nothing for `ol`. As a result, WebKit / Safari and Blink / Chrome fails these tests.\r\n\r\nI have raised this bug on WebKit side and can fix it: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=265619\r\n\r\nBut I just wanted to raise here to get insight, whether we should extend 'presentational hints' to 'ol' or update test and test 'ul', which is not tested yet.\r\n\r\nLooking forward for insight and input.\r\n\r\nThanks!",
